 describing the number of customers for each smartphone is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}600\\,000 \\\\ 400\\,000\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nDividing the vector above by the total number of customers $(1\\,000\\,000),$ we get the stochastic vector of the initial state:\n\n$$\n{x}_{0}=\\frac{1}{1\\,000\\,000}\\begin{bmatrix}600\\,000 \\\\ 400\\,000\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0.6 \\\\ 0.4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo find the state vector ${x}_{1}$ after one year, we apply one step of the Markov chain:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=P{x}_{0}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =P{x}_{0} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.6 & 0.3 \\\\ 0.4 & 0.7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0.6 \\\\ 0.4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.48 \\\\ 0.52\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after one year, $48%$ of customers will use Phone $A.$ Computing $48%$ of $1\\,000\\,000,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n1\\,000\\,000\\cdot 0.48=480\\,000.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $480\\,000$ customers will use Phone $A$ in one year." 13194139536171 17592186045443 false] [17592186124924 1074 "From the table, we can build the corresponding stochastic matrix: \n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0.6 & 0.3 \\\\ 0.4 & 0.7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe vector describing the number of customers for each smartphone is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}600\\,000 \\\\ 400\\,000\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nDividing the vector above by the total number of customers $(1\\,000\\,000),$ we get the stochastic vector of the initial state:\n\n$$\n{x}_{0}=\\frac{1}{1\\,000\\,000}\\begin{bmatrix}600\\,000 \\\\ 400\\,000\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0.6 \\\\ 0.4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo find the state vector ${x}_{1}$ after one year, we apply one step of the Markov chain:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=P{x}_{0}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =P{x}_{0} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.6 & 0.3 \\\\ 0.4 & 0.7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0.6 \\\\ 0.4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.48 \\\\ 0.52\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after one year, $48\\%$ of customers will use Phone $A.$ Computing $48\\%$ of $1\\,000\\,000,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n1\\,000\\,000\\cdot 0.48=480\\,000.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $480\\,000$ customers will use Phone $A$ in one year." 13194139536171 17592186045443 true] [17592186125144 1071 "Let $T:{R}^{4}\\to {R}^{4}$ be a linear transformation whose standard matrix is $T.$ Consider the following statement:\n\n*If $T$ is invertible, then $\\text{__________}.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n- **I.** $\\text{Ker}(T)={0}$\n- **II.** $\\text{rank}(T)\\ne 4$\n- **III.** $\\text{nullity}(T)\\ne 0$\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139536171 17592186045443 false] [17592186125144 1071 "Let $T:{R}^{4}\\to {R}^{4}$ be a linear transformation whose standard matrix is $T.$ Consider the following statement:\n\n*If $T$ is invertible, then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n- **I.** $\\text{Ker}(T)={0}$\n- **II.** $\\text{rank}(T)\\ne 4$\n- **III.** $\\text{nullity}(T)\\ne 0$\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139536171 17592186045443 true] [17592186125164 1071 "Let $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ be a linear transformation whose standard matrix is $T.$ Consider the following statement:\n\n*If $[1,-1]^{T}\\notin \\text{Im}(T)$, then $\\text{__________}.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\n- **I.** $\\text{Ker}(T)=\\{0\\}$\n\n- **II.** $\\text{rank}(T)\\ne 2$\n\n- **III.** $T$ is invertible\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139536171 17592186045443 false] [17592186125164 1071 "Let $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ be a linear transformation whose standard matrix is $T.$ Consider the following statement:\n\n*If $[1,-1]^{T}\\notin \\text{Im}(T)$, then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\n- **I.** $\\text{Ker}(T)=\\{0\\}$\n\n- **II.** $\\text{rank}(T)\\ne 2$\n\n- **III.*